    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d79">

                <pb facs="0160" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg92"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1986.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 20, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 2d of May, No. 1361,
                    has been received. There is no reason why you should not give Lord Stanley a
                    full copy of my despatch No. 1965.</p>
                <pb facs="0161" n="93" xml:id="pg93"/>
                <p>My confidential despatch of May 2d, No. 1971, will have removed from your mind
                    any impression that the President may be expected to accede to the limitation
                    upon the arbitration of the Alabama claims which Lord Stanley proposed.</p>
                <p>The United States are thus in the attitude of insisting upon the claims, as they
                    have consistently done from the beginning, and of declining to accede to
                    arbitration thereupon with limitations hitherto insisted upon by her Majesty’s
                    government.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
